# Which backend the app talks to (EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL). Restart `bunx expo start` after changing it.
#
# Development (Expo Go): put it in .env.development.local, which only `expo start` reads.
#   Unset = the backend on the computer running Expo (port 3000).
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://droin-api.zoelunels.my.id
#
# Release APK built on this computer (gradlew assembleRelease): .env.production.
# EAS builds: eas.json. Don't use plain .env.local: release builds read it too, and it wins over
# .env.production, so a dev address would end up in the APK.
